# Worker: Investigator LLM & Prompts

## Goal (Master-aligned)

Own **optional** Groq/Ollama enrichment, prompts, and LLM config. IR drafting stays PDF-backed; LLM is never required for a valid Investigate → Report path.

## Role boundary

**Own:** `investigator_llm.py`, `investigator_prompt.py`, LLM flags/config, `.env.example` placeholders, model-id churn (403/404/limit) UX for operators.

**Do not own:** subsection ranking, quote verification, IR shell/DOCX, corpus ingest, PrivacyGate UI — consume their outputs only.

## Invariants

- `LLM_FOR_INVESTIGATE` defaults **false** — off the critical IR path
- LLM is **enrichment only** of already-scoped context (approved codes + PDF-backed material)
- LLM must **never** choose subsections or supply authoritative statute quote text
- Sole-source `data/source/` PDFs win over any LLM output (Master conflict rule)
- Never invent or paraphrase law as if from the store; never commit real API keys

## Anti-goals

- Making LLM the default or required Investigate path
- Using model free-text as authority for codes, subsections, or quotes
- Silent fallback that invents statute wording when the model fails
- Bypassing Privacy redact-before-LLM contracts

## Success criteria

- Default-off path produces IR drafts without calling the model
- When enabled, enrichment is clearly non-authoritative and scoped
- Failures are actionable (missing key, retired model) — no invented law
- Prompts instruct: do not invent citations/quotes; defer to PDF-backed inputs

## Escalation map

| Signal | Escalate to |
|--------|-------------|
| Allegation/quote/IR shell/DOCX | IR Drafting |
| Ranking / PDF ingest wrong | Statute Corpus |
| PII before LLM call | Privacy & PII |
| Accuracy / goldens after prompt changes | Accuracy & Eval |
| Ports / Launch / debug env | Local DevEx |

Return the standard handoff block from `AGENTS.md`.
